[Music]  hello games has launched the newest free  update for no man sky called next the  update makes massive overhauls for the  game by adding multiplayer character  customization command freighters and  more  although the core exploration mechanics  remain intact next pretty much  transforms no man's sky into a  completely different game in this video  we've outlined the biggest changes  thanks to next you can now join up with  random strangers or team up with a small  contingent of friends to construct  colonies of small shelters race EXO  craft or engage in space battles help  differentiate between avatars next adds  character customization so that everyone  can personalize their in-game appearance  you'll be able to switch up your species  and change your outfits and hairstyles  to not everyone you meet is a friendly  face though so when you run into another  player in the midst of exploring the  Stars it's best to be cautious a  collection of ships approaching on the  horizon might be a crew of players  helping to steal your loot of course if  you've got the nerve for it you can  become a space pirate yourself  [Music]  you'll be able to invite your friends  onto your very own command freighter to  tackle challenging multiplayer missions  and if you're still having trouble  you'll be able to build and upgrade a  whole fleet of frigates which you can  then customize to specialize in combat  exploration trade industry or support  you can use what you found to build  bases which can now be constructed  anywhere on any planet you'll even be  able to build on top of mountains and  beneath the sea and if you don't like  how the terrain is affecting the shape  of your base the improved terrain  manipulator allows players to sculpt the  planet's surface to their needs the  manipulator can be used to excavate  ancient treasures - which can be sold in  the new space station marketplace the  resources used to customize your fleet  and basis as well as craft your gear and  equipment have all been reworked and  rebalance many of the resources you  remember from the original no man sky  have received new names and be given  completely different uses  we hope you haven't memorized the full  assortment of uses for the materials  that compose gnome and skies original  periodic table because most of that  information is useless man  the opening section of no man's sky has  been updated with new story elements as  well as a tutorial that teaches advanced  gameplay features mission chains help  get players started with exploring  planets and starting basis once passed  the tutorial new types of missions are  available to complete new photography  feeding freighter attack and defense  archaeology and hunting missions expand  the amount of activities that players  can do players won't be getting all of  their objectives from the same merchant  either as next adds a diverse assortment  of random NPCs on different stations as  quest givers  the visuals to no man's sky have also  gotten an overhaul terrain generates  faster and groundwater and cloud  textures have been upgraded ships NPCs  and buildings have more detail to no  man's sky is also now fully playable in  both first and third person whether  you're walking on the surface of a  planet or shooting your way through a  dogma draw distance has been improved so  plants appear more dense and a new color  palette paints the forest oceans and  plains of each world with added vibrancy  the creatures you'll discover on your  travels will now act more  enthusiastically towards you if you feed  them letting you herd them together  the creatures AI has also been revamped  so they act more intelligently  responding to players they recognize as  friendly and fleeing as a group from a  perceived danger not all the new animals  and plant life are friendly however keep  on the lookout for new hazardous species  as they will kill you if you're not  careful plenty of us here at GameSpot  have jumped back into no man's sky to  play the next update which of the  changes are convincing you to give hello  game space explore and never go leave  your responses in the comment section  below and let us know what you're  discovering on your adventures with your  friends  no man skies designer Shaun Murray has  been tweeting about updates made to the  game that aren't included in next patch  notes has us thinking that the new  update is hiding a few secrets that  players will just have to discover on  their own let you know if we find any so  be sure to keep checking back on  gamespot for all things no man's sky  [Music]

